course: dictionary
lesson: 5321
title: Kenyan: a person, and a word for things from Kenya
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Kenyan can work in two ways. A Kenyan is a person who comes from Kenya, a country in East Africa. Kenyan can also describe things that belong to Kenya or its people, such as Kenyan food or Kenyan wildlife.
explain: Look at the words around it to decide which way it works. «Kenyan runners often win long-distance races.» Here Kenyan describes the runners, so it is describing word. In «English belongs to everyone who speaks it: ... a Kenyan, Nigerian or Indian speaker may have spoken it all their life», a Kenyan is a person, so it is a noun.
explain: Always write Kenyan with a capital K, because it names a country and its people. Try swapping in another country name: «a Kenyan speaker» could become «a Nigerian speaker», and the sentence still makes sense. That tells you Kenyan works like a name.
fact: Kenya is a country in East Africa.
fact: Kenya's capital city is Nairobi.
fact: Mount Kenya, the Great Rift Valley and safari parks are all in Kenya.
fact: Kenyan runners often win long-distance races.
exercise: Who is a Kenyan? | A kind of long-distance race | *A person who comes from Kenya, a country in East Africa | A large wild animal from the African plains | A person who lives in a big city in Europe
exercise: «Kenyan runners often win long-distance races.» What does Kenyan mean in this sentence? | *Belonging to Kenya or its people | Very fast | Found in the sea | Made of wood
exercise: What is the capital city of Kenya? | *Nairobi | Lagos | London | Cairo
test: In the phrase «a Kenyan runner», what kind of word is Kenyan? | adverb | *adjective | verb | noun
test: Which of these is a place in Kenya? | The Alps | Mount Everest | *Mount Kenya | Ben Nevis
exam: What is the plural noun for more than one person from Kenya? | Kenyaners | *Kenyans | Kenyas | Kenyan
